    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=The vendor is '{{ $json.company_name }}' with domain '{{ $json.vendor_domain }}'. What is the most likely GitHub organization slug for this company? Consider: exact company name, company name without spaces/special chars, domain root. Return ONLY a JSON object with this exact shape: {\"candidate_slugs\": [\"slug1\",\"slug2\",\"slug3\"], \"confidence\": \"low|medium|high\", \"reasoning\": \"short\"}. If the company is unlikely to have a GitHub org (small consultancy, legacy ERP, etc.), return {\"candidate_slugs\": [], \"confidence\": \"low\", \"reasoning\": \"why\"}. Order candidates most likely first, max 3.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
